# Daily Vivaldi Social auto-poster

Posts one fresh AI/tech news headline + link to your Vivaldi Social
account every day, automatically — no server of your own needed.

## 1. Get an access token
On Vivaldi Social: **Preferences → Development → New Application**
- Name: `daily-poster` (or anything)
- Scopes: at least `write:statuses`
- Create, then copy the **access token** it gives you.

## 2. Put these files in a GitHub repo
```
your-repo/
├── daily_poster.py
├── requirements.txt
├── posted_links.json      (create as empty: [])
└── .github/
    └── workflows/
        └── daily-post.yml   (rename from daily-post.yml above)
```

## 3. Add repo secrets
Repo → **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret**
- `VIVALDI_ACCESS_TOKEN` = the token from step 1
- `VIVALDI_INSTANCE_URL` = `https://vivaldi.social` (or your instance's URL)

## 4. Done
GitHub Actions will run the script daily on its own schedule (edit the
`cron` line in the workflow to change the time — it's in UTC). You can
also trigger a test run manually from the repo's **Actions** tab any
time via "Run workflow".

## Notes / easy tweaks
- **Change news sources:** edit the `FEEDS` list in `daily_poster.py` —
  any RSS feed works (add your own interests, not just AI/tech).
- **Post images too:** Mastodon's `/api/v1/media` endpoint uploads an
  image first, then you attach its returned ID to the status — say the
  word if you want this added.
- **No repeats:** `posted_links.json` tracks what's already been
  shared, so it won't post the same story twice.
- **Local test run instead of GitHub Actions:**
  ```
  pip install -r requirements.txt
  export VIVALDI_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_token
  export VIVALDI_INSTANCE_URL=https://vivaldi.social
  python daily_poster.py
  ```
